# Feature structure (The Composable Architecture)

Every screen in `Features` is a **TCA feature** — a reducer + a SwiftUI view. Two
files in the feature's folder:

```
Features/Sources/Features/Home/
  HomeFeature.swift   # @Reducer: State + Action + body
  HomeView.swift      # SwiftUI view driven by StoreOf<HomeFeature> + #Preview
```

The `Home*` pair is the reference implementation.

## Reducer (`{Feature}Feature.swift`)

```kotlin
@Reducer
public struct HomeFeature {
    @ObservableState
    public struct State: Equatable { public var isLoading = true; public init() {} }

    public enum Action {
        case task
        case greetingResponse(Greeting)
        case delegate(Delegate)
        @CasePathable public enum Delegate: Equatable { case openDetails(id: String) }
    }

    @Dependency(\.platformInfo) private var platformInfo

    public var body: some ReducerOf<Self> {
        Reduce { state, action in /* single switch */ }
    }
}
```

- `State` is `@ObservableState` and `Equatable`; holds **durable UI state only** — no one-shot flags.
- `Action` is a flat enum. Side effects return `.run { }`; navigation/parent signals go through a
  nested `@CasePathable enum Delegate` case, never a boolean in State.
- Dependencies come via `@Dependency(\.…)` (a `:Domain` client) — never import `Data` or call a device API.
- `public` the types + members that the app/tests use (it is a library package).

## View (`{Feature}View.swift`)

- `@Bindable var store: StoreOf<{Feature}>`, a `public init(store:)`, no business logic.
- Read `store.<state>`; send `store.send(.action)`. Kick off loads with `.task { store.send(.task) }`.
- `#Preview` in the same file (see `swiftui-previews`). Use `:Styleguide` components/tokens.

## Composition & navigation

Screens are composed in `AppFeature` (root reducer) with a type-safe navigation stack — see the
`navigation` rule. A child signals the parent via `delegate`; the parent `Scope`s children and drives
`StackState`.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Navigation/alert state as `Bool`/optional flags in `State` instead of an `Action`/`@Presents`
- ❌ A view holding business logic or resolving a dependency directly
- ❌ Importing `Data` or UIKit from `Features`
- ❌ A reducer without a single exhaustive `switch` in `Reduce`
